## Rebuilding dotfiles from this audit

Recommended workflow:

\`1.\` Create a fresh dotfiles branch/repo.  
\`2.\` Review \`raw/packages/pacman-modified-backups.txt\` and \`raw/packages/etc-unowned.txt\`.  
\`3.\` Copy only intentionally maintained files from \`snapshot$HOME/.config/...\` and selected \`snapshot/etc/...\`.  
\`4.\` Turn the package lists into a bootstrap script (\`pacman -S --needed ...\` plus your AUR helper).  
\`5.\` Turn enabled services into explicit \`systemctl enable ...\` / \`systemctl --user enable ...\` bootstrap steps.  
\`6.\` Keep hardware- or machine-specific files (monitor EDIDs, hostnames, fstab UUIDs, network profiles) separate from portable dotfiles.  
\`7.\` Never commit the whole audit directory blindly, especially after using \`--include-sensitive\`.
EOF

if [[ -n "$DOTFILES_DIR" ]]; then
  cat >> "$REPORT" <<EOF

## Existing dotfiles repo

Repo: \`$DOTFILES_DIR\`

- [Git status/remotes](raw/dotfiles/repo.txt)
- [Symlinks resolving into the repo](raw/dotfiles/symlinks-into-repo.txt)

EOF
fi

if (( FULL )); then
  printf \
    '\nFull pacman integrity scan (`pacman -Qkk`) was enabled.\n' \
    >> "$REPORT"
else
  printf \
    '\nFor a slower package integrity pass, re-run with `--full`.\n' \
    >> "$REPORT"
fi

cat > "$OUT/compare-current.sh" <<'EOF'
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

ROOT="$(
  cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")"
  pwd
)"

if [[ $# -ne 1 || "$1" != /* ]]; then
  echo "Usage: $0 /absolute/path/to/config" >&2
  exit 2
fi

snap="$ROOT/snapshot$1"

if [[ ! -e "$snap" && ! -L "$snap" ]]; then
  echo "Not found in snapshot: $snap" >&2
  exit 1
fi

diff \
  -u \
  -- \
  "$snap" \
  "$1" ||
  true
EOF

chmod +x "$OUT/compare-current.sh"

if have tar; then
  (
    cd "$OUTPUT_BASE"

    tar \
      -czf "${HOST}-${STAMP}.tar.gz" \
      "${HOST}-${STAMP}"
  ) 2>>"$ERRORS" || true
fi

log "Done."

printf '\nReport:   %s\n' "$REPORT"
printf 'Snapshot: %s\n' "$SNAPSHOT"
printf 'Manifest: %s\n' "$MANIFEST"

if [[ -f "${OUTPUT_BASE%/}/${HOST}-${STAMP}.tar.gz" ]]; then
  printf \
    'Archive:  %s\n' \
    "${OUTPUT_BASE%/}/${HOST}-${STAMP}.tar.gz"
fi

printf '\nReview REPORT.md first. Do not commit the audit directory wholesale.\n'
